{"kind":"artifact","text":"Documentation for #11107 at docs/reference/gs/merge.md@0428e915bdd61de747709b810af9ad5881fe645e on branch request/sealed-receipt-directional-resume. The directional-reach section now states the check belongs to fresh merges only and runs once, in preflight, before the merge commit exists, before HEAD moves, and before anything durable is written, with succession recording never re-applying it; resuming an interrupted merge appends the immutable recorded suffix without replanning and without this guard, so a receipt sealed under an older reading of reach keeps exactly the authority it was sealed with. The prior text's claim that first completion re-checks the plan is removed as false of the repaired surface.","body":{"branch":"request/sealed-receipt-directional-resume","commit":"0428e915bdd61de747709b810af9ad5881fe645e","head":"0428e915bdd61de747709b810af9ad5881fe645e","path":"docs/reference/gs/merge.md"}}